---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="API reference">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-12">
    <a href="/" class="text-xs text-slate-500 hover:text-oxblood-700">← Back to docs</a>
    <h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-900">API reference</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-base text-slate-600">
      The Driftstack HTTP API surface lives at <span class="font-mono">https://api.driftstack.dev</span>.
      Every endpoint is versioned under <span class="font-mono">/v1/*</span>; new majors land
      with explicit deprecation cycles per the policy below.
    </p>

    <ul class="mt-8 space-y-4 text-sm text-slate-700">
      <li>
        <span class="font-medium text-slate-900">OpenAPI spec.</span>
        Live at <span class="font-mono">/openapi.json</span>; rendered via Scalar at
        <span class="font-mono">/docs/</span> on the API host.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="font-medium text-slate-900">Versioning policy.</span>
        Detailed at
        <a
          href="https://github.com/driftstackdev/driftstack-api/blob/main/docs/architecture/api-versioning.md"
          class="text-oxblood-700 hover:underline"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">docs/architecture/api-versioning.md</a
        > in the repository (V-220). One major active at a time; additive changes are free; breaking
        changes go through a 90-day deprecation cycle.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="font-medium text-slate-900">Webhook events.</span>
        Catalog of every event type the API emits at
        <a
          href="https://github.com/driftstackdev/driftstack-api/blob/main/docs/api/webhook-events.md"
          class="text-oxblood-700 hover:underline"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">docs/api/webhook-events.md</a
        > (V-203).
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="font-medium text-slate-900">Authentication.</span>
        Bearer API keys (<span class="font-mono">ds_live_…</span> for production,
        <span class="font-mono">ds_test_…</span> for trial-pack tier). Web sessions on the customer
        dashboard use opaque sha256-hashed tokens (D-028); Bearer header in both cases.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="mt-10 text-sm text-slate-500">
      Pre-launch — full per-endpoint pages migrate from the repository
      <span class="font-mono">/docs/</span> tree in subsequent doc-site releases.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
